  "name": "Cantes de ida y vuelta (guajira, colombiana, milonga)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The cantes de ida y vuelta ('there-and-back songs') are the flamenco palos shaped from Latin American song that travelled back to Andalusian ports: the guajira from Cuba, the milonga and vidalita from the River Plate, and the colombiana, which Pepe Marchena composed on Latin American models. Marchena's 78-rpm records of colombianas and guajiras and Juanito Valderrama's milongas made them popular.",
  "recipe": "classic Iberian early-1950s cantes de ida y vuelta, ballad Poetry, Mediterranean ballad branch. single lead single track no stacking. cypress body percussive attack strong flamenco tradition low action golpe tap plate flamenco guitar. andalusian tablao seville madrid. Neumann U47, tube pre, colored vintage console, LA-2A optical, passive program EQ. tape 15ips plate reverb.",
